.TH "dotclean" "1" "August 2026" "" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dotclean \- merge or remove AppleDouble \f[CR]._*\f[R] sidecar files
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]dotclean\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]] \f[I]directory\f[R] \&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]dotclean\f[R] is a cross\-platform reimplementation of macOS
\f[B]dot_clean\f[R](1).
For each \f[I]directory\f[R], it finds AppleDouble sidecar files (names
beginning with \f[CR]._\f[R]) and either merges their metadata into the
corresponding native file or discards that metadata, then optionally
deletes the sidecar.
.PP
\f[B]Merge\f[R] (apply extended attributes from the AppleDouble file) is
performed \f[B]only\f[R] on \f[B]HFS+\f[R] and \f[B]APFS\f[R] volumes.
On all other filesystems\[em]including \f[B]FAT32\f[R] and
\f[B]exFAT\f[R]\[em]metadata cannot be stored natively without
recreating a \f[CR]._*\f[R] file, so \f[B]dotclean\f[R] discards the
sidecar contents and deletes the sidecar (unless \f[B]\[en]preserve\f[R]
is set).
Missing extended\-attribute support is not an error; a successful
cleanup exits 0.
Merge never applies \f[B]com.apple.macl\f[R] or
\f[B]com.apple.provenance\f[R]; \f[B]com.apple.quarantine\f[R] is
applied only with \f[B]\-Q\f[R].
Permission errors setting an attribute are skipped so other attributes
can still be written.
.PP
Unlike Apple\[cq]s tool, path operands are treated as opaque: whitespace
inside a single argument is preserved.
.PP
\f[CR].DS_Store\f[R] and other Finder litter are \f[B]not\f[R] removed
in the default (normal) mode.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-f\f[R], \f[B]\[en]flat\f[R]
Do not recurse into subdirectories.
.TP
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\[en]help\f[R]
Print help and exit.
.TP
\f[B]\-m\f[R], \f[B]\[en]always\-delete\f[R]
Always delete AppleDouble files (including orphans).
Overrides \f[B]\[en]preserve\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-n\f[R], \f[B]\[en]cleanup\f[R]
Delete an AppleDouble file if there is no matching native file.
.TP
\f[B]\-p\f[R], \f[B]\[en]preserve\f[R]
Preserve AppleDouble files after handling (do not delete paired
sidecars).
.TP
\f[B]\-s\f[R], \f[B]\[en]follow\-symlinks\f[R]
Follow symbolic links when they point at AppleDouble files.
.TP
\f[B]\-v\f[R], \f[B]\[en]verbose\f[R]
Print verbose progress to standard error.
.TP
\f[B]\-N\f[R], \f[B]\[en]dry\-run\f[R]
List paths that would be deleted; do not merge or delete anything.
.TP
\f[B]\-Q\f[R], \f[B]\[en]set\-quarantine\f[R]
When merging on HFS+/APFS, apply \f[B]com.apple.quarantine\f[R] from the
AppleDouble sidecar.
Off by default (matches Apple \f[B]dot_clean\f[R], which does not
re\-apply quarantine).
.TP
\f[B]\[en]keep\f[R]=\f[I]mode\f[R]
When merging on HFS+/APFS: \f[B]mostrecent\f[R] (default; prefer
existing native attributes), \f[B]dotbar\f[R] (prefer AppleDouble), or
\f[B]native\f[R] (skip applying AppleDouble attributes).
