.SH EXAMPLES
Remove AppleDouble sidecars under a USB volume (typical FAT/exFAT
cleanup):
.IP
.EX
dotclean /Volumes/USB
.EE
.PP
Preview deletions:
.IP
.EX
dotclean \-N \[dq]/media/user/My Drive/Pictures\[dq]
.EE
.PP
Merge preferring AppleDouble data on an APFS path, then delete sidecars:
.IP
.EX
dotclean \-\-keep=dotbar \[ti]/Documents
.EE
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
\f[B]dotclean\f[R] exits 0 on success (including a successful dry\-run),
and >0 if an error occurs.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[B]dot_clean\f[R](1) on macOS, AppleSingle/AppleDouble Formats (Apple
Developer Note).
.SH NOTES
This implementation is not affiliated with Apple.
Behavior aims to match useful \f[B]dot_clean\f[R] semantics for
removable media while fixing path whitespace handling and documenting
\f[B]\[en]preserve\f[R] (\f[B]\-p\f[R]), which appears in Apple\[cq]s
\f[B]\-h\f[R] output but not always in the published man page.
